---
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";

const facts = [
  "Platform engineer, most comfortable in Python and Go",
  "Cloud as code: GCP & AWS with Terraform · Kubernetes · GitOps",
  "Observability: Datadog, Prometheus, Grafana",
  "Spanish & Italian citizen (EU) · Madrid · open to relocate",
];
---

<Section id="about" prompt="~/about" title="About">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_320px] lg:items-start">
    <div class="space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
      <p>
        I'm a platform engineer who gravitates toward the layer where systems
        stay up: infrastructure as code, Kubernetes, CI/CD and observability.
        At Saab I diagnosed a critical failover flaw in a mission-critical,
        on-prem VoIP system and designed its cloud-native Active/Active
        replacement on AWS EKS. The work won Best Engineering Internship of
        the Year from the Danish National Academies and a public endorsement
        from Saab's Head of Platform Engineering.
      </p>
      <p>
        Day to day that means GCP and AWS managed as code with Terraform,
        quality gates in CI, Datadog and Prometheus telling me the truth
        about production, and AI-assisted development used daily (agents
        included), building genuine fluency rather than surface-level use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Off the clock I run a tailnet-only homelab and work through
        HackTheBox labs, because understanding how systems break is how you
        learn to keep them up. Full write-ups and postmortems land on this
        site as they happen. Still early in my career, and genuinely
        motivated to keep improving: new tools when they help, teammates who
        know more than I do whenever I can find them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Beyond the terminal: skis in winter, a bouldering wall year-round,
        and enthusiastic attempts at surfing that the ocean graciously does
        not grade.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside
      class="p-0 font-mono text-sm sm:rounded-xl sm:border sm:border-zinc-700/60 sm:bg-zinc-900 sm:p-5"
      aria-label="Quick facts"
    >
      <p class="text-zinc-500">$ facts --brief</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2.5">
        {
          facts.map((fact) => (
            <li class="flex gap-2 text-zinc-300">
              <span class="select-none text-zinc-600">→</span>
              {fact}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Section>
